Pizza Legacy v@PROJECT_VERSION@ - macOS Release (Apple Silicon)
====================================================

Pizza Legacy is an open-source reimplementation of the 1994 DOS game
Pizza Connection/Pizza Tycoon.

FIRST LAUNCH – macOS security message
--------------------------------------

On recent versions of macOS, you may see a message saying:

    "Pizza Legacy" is damaged and can’t be opened.
     You should move it to the Bin.

This is a macOS security restriction (Gatekeeper) that appears because
the app is not signed with an Apple Developer certificate.

The app is not actually damaged.

To allow it to run, open Terminal and run:

    xattr -cr "/path/to/Pizza Legacy.app"

Tip: You can type `xattr -cr ` (with a space), then drag the app into
Terminal to fill in the path automatically.

Then try opening the app again.

You only need to do this once.

Alternative method (if available):

After attempting to open the app once, go to:
System Settings -> Privacy & Security

If an "Open Anyway" option appears (near the bottom), you can use that instead.


REQUIREMENTS
------------
The game requires the asset files from the original Pizza Tycoon /
Pizza Connection. Point the game at your installation directory on
first launch (the folder containing PT.EXE).

The original game (Pizza Connection) is available on GOG and Steam,
frequently on sale for under a euro.


STATUS
------
Alpha. Expect rough edges and missing features. Development is active.
See https://pizzalegacy.nl/ for current status.

Find the full README online:
https://codeberg.org/cowomaly/pizzalegacy/src/branch/main/README.md


THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
--------------------
This build includes third-party libraries (SDL2, libpng, libADLMIDI).
Their individual licenses are included inside the app bundle at:

    Pizza Legacy.app/Contents/Resources/LICENSES/

Right-click the app and choose "Show Package Contents" to browse it.

A summary of all third-party components can be found in `THIRD_PARTIES.txt`.

